#{[17592186561368 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186561330 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186561368 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186561368 #edb/ref 1071 "If $f(x,y)=x e^{x y},$ $x=(t - 3)^{2}$ and $y=(t - 1)^{2},$ compute $\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}t}$." #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186561368 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "c1b4aee3-81b2-5ef4-a432-21293ceb4d7a" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186561368 #edb/ref 1074 "![](images/f0/f01b253f560405a8c0f4be8f8797c652fb0ddf774f4db110b8822313b8ac50f3.png)\n\nThe chain rule for a multivariable function $f(x,y)$ with one independent variable $t,$ where $x=x(t)$ and $y=y(t),$ can be expressed as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}t}=\\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives of $f$ with respect to $x$ and $y:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} &=x y e^{x y} + e^{x y},\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=x^{2} e^{x y}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWriting the above results in terms of $t,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =(t - 3)^{2} (t - 1)^{2} e^{(t - 3)^{2} (t - 1)^{2}} + e^{(t - 3)^{2} (t - 1)^{2}} \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =(t - 3)^{4} e^{(t - 3)^{2} (t - 1)^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we take the derivatives of $x$ and $y$ with respect to $t,$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t} &=2 t - 6,\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}=2 t - 2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting all of our derivatives into the multivariable chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =((t - 3)^{2} (t - 1)^{2} e^{(t - 3)^{2} (t - 1)^{2}} + e^{(t - 3)^{2} (t - 1)^{2}})\\cdot (2 t - 6)+((t - 3)^{4} e^{(t - 3)^{2} (t - 1)^{2}})\\cdot (2 t - 2) \\\\  & =(2 t - 6) e^{(t - 3)^{2} (t - 1)^{2}} + ((t - 3)^{2} (t - 1)^{2} (2 t - 6) e^{(t - 3)^{2} (t - 1)^{2}}) + ((t - 3)^{4} (2 t - 2) e^{(t - 3)^{2} (t - 1)^{2}}) \\\\  & =2 (t - 3) ((t - 3)^{3} (t - 1) + (t - 3)^{2} (t - 1)^{2} + 1) e^{(t - 3)^{2} (t - 1)^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186561373 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186561370 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186561373 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186561373 #edb/ref 1071 "If $f(x,y)=x e^{x y},$ $x=(2 t - 1)^{3}$ and $y=(2 t - 2)^{2},$ compute $\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}t}$." #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186561373 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "df6ac8b1-d356-59b7-bc1d-0aa4d063c094" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186561373 #edb/ref 1074 "![](images/f0/f01b253f560405a8c0f4be8f8797c652fb0ddf774f4db110b8822313b8ac50f3.png)\n\nThe chain rule for a multivariable function $f(x,y)$ with one independent variable $t,$ where $x=x(t)$ and $y=y(t),$ can be expressed as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}t}=\\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives of $f$ with respect to $x$ and $y:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} &=x y e^{x y} + e^{x y},\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=x^{2} e^{x y}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWriting the above results in terms of $t,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =(2 t - 2)^{2} (2 t - 1)^{3} e^{(2 t - 2)^{2} (2 t - 1)^{3}} + e^{(2 t - 2)^{2} (2 t - 1)^{3}} \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =(2 t - 1)^{6} e^{(2 t - 2)^{2} (2 t - 1)^{3}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we take the derivatives of $x$ and $y$ with respect to $t,$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t} &=6 (2 t - 1)^{2},\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}=8 t - 8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting all of our derivatives into the multivariable chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =((2 t - 2)^{2} (2 t - 1)^{3} e^{(2 t - 2)^{2} (2 t - 1)^{3}} + e^{(2 t - 2)^{2} (2 t - 1)^{3}})\\cdot (6 (2 t - 1)^{2})+((2 t - 1)^{6} e^{(2 t - 2)^{2} (2 t - 1)^{3}})\\cdot (8 t - 8) \\\\  & =6 (2 t - 1)^{2} e^{(2 t - 2)^{2} (2 t - 1)^{3}} + (6 (2 t - 2)^{2} (2 t - 1)^{5} e^{(2 t - 2)^{2} (2 t - 1)^{3}}) + ((2 t - 1)^{6} (8 t - 8) e^{(2 t - 2)^{2} (2 t - 1)^{3}}) \\\\  & =2 (2 t - 1)^{2} (12 (t - 1)^{2} (2 t - 1)^{3} + 4 (t - 1) (2 t - 1)^{4} + 3) e^{(2 t - 2)^{2} (2 t - 1)^{3}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186561381 #edb/ref 1168 "generate/scratch/17592186166747.py" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186561381 #edb/ref 1169 #uuid "4f3229b7-d188-5de9-bf1b-a0c92e77f8fd" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186565663 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186566279 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186565663 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186566302 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186565663 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186566307 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186565663 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186566315 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186565663 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186566320 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186565663 #edb/ref 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045464 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186565663 #edb/ref 1045 "The Multivariable Chain Rule" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186565663 #edb/ref 1046 #edb/ref 17592186566320 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186565663 #edb/ref 1048 #edb/ref 17592186046668 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186565663 #edb/ref 1049 #edb/ref 17592186050031 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186565663 #edb/ref 1053 #uuid "09f63cf7-87d6-50ff-b17a-338839a04aa8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186565671 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186566295 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186565671 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186566304 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186565671 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186566306 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186565671 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186566318 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186565671 #edb/ref 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045460 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [1759