[17592186566177 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186566022 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186566177 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186566177 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186566177 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186565884 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186566177 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "bb17ec4b-63ee-5206-af27-3498015a3fd6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186566273 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186566177 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186566273 #edb/ref 1069 "q-163179" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186566273 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186566273 #edb/ref 1071 "A rectangular plate occupies the region\n$D=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 2,\\,0\\le y\\le 3\\}$\nand has mass density function $\\lambda (x,y)=y,$ where $x$ and $y$ are measured in meters.\nGiven that the center of mass is at $(1,2),$ find the moment of inertia about a line perpendicular to $D$ at a distance of $\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\,\\text{m}$ from a parallel line passing through its center of mass." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186566273 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "f7c6f3ba-6533-5a1f-b464-492440ca8f6d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186566273 #edb/ref 1074 "For a plane lamina of mass $M$ and a line ${l}_{M}$ perpendicular to the lamina passing through its center of mass, the parallel axis theorem states that the moment of inertia of the lamina about a line $l$ parallel to ${l}_{M}$ is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{l}={I}_{M}+{d}^{2}M,\n$$\n\nwhere $d$ is the distance between the lines, and ${I}_{M}$ and ${I}_{l}$ are the moments of inertia about the lines ${l}_{M}$ and $l,$ respectively.\n\nFirst, we find the mass of the plate as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{3}y\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x{\\int }_{0}^{3}y\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =x{|}_{0}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}{y}^{2}{|}_{0}^{3} \\\\  & =2\\cdot \\frac{9}{2} \\\\  & =9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, the moment of inertia about the perpendicular line through the center of mass $(1,2)$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{M} & ={∬}_{D}((x-\\overset{¯}{x})^{2}+(y-\\overset{¯}{y})^{2})\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}((x-1)^{2}+(y-2)^{2})\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{3}((x-1)^{2}+(y-2)^{2})y\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{3}(x-1)^{2}y+{y}^{3}-4{y}^{2}+4y\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{[\\frac{1}{2}(x-1)^{2}{y}^{2}+\\frac{1}{4}{y}^{4}-\\frac{4}{3}{y}^{3}+2{y}^{2}]}_{y=0}^{y=3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{9}{2}(x-1)^{2}+\\frac{9}{4}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[\\frac{3}{2}(x-1)^{3}+\\frac{9}{4}x]}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}+\\frac{9}{2}-(-\\frac{3}{2}+0) \\\\  & =\\frac{15}{2}\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, applying the parallel axis theorem, the moment of inertia about a line $\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\,\\text{m}$ from the center of mass is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & ={I}_{M}+{d}^{2}M \\\\  & =\\frac{15}{2}+{(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2})}^{2}\\cdot 9 \\\\  & =\\frac{15}{2}+\\frac{9}{2} \\\\  & =12\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186566279 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186566302 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186566279 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "0fd6e11a-f464-5bf8-9292-0f8d1c7bae19" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186566279 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186360558 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186566295 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186566318 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186566295 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "6473ded1-3ff1-56db-b8af-a5723874b273" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186566295 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186360483 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186566302 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186566307 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186566302 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "9adfb7c9-467c-5ab8-90bb-dc9e969772c0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186566302 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 1759218